Phos-Flur Rinse contains sodium fluoride at a concentration of 0.044% (w/v). How many milligrams of sodium fluoride are present in a 10 mL dose?,"<bos><start_of_turn>user
Phos-Flur Rinse contains sodium fluoride at a concentration of 0.044% (w/v). How many milligrams of sodium fluoride are present in a 10 mL dose?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the percentage to a fraction:**  
   0.044% = 0.044 / 100 = 0.00044

2. **Interpret the units (w/v):**  
   (w/v) means weight per volume, where the volume is in milliliters (mL) and the weight is in grams (g).  
   So, 0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of Phos-Flur Rinse.

3. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**  
   If 100 mL contains 0.044 g, then 10 mL contains:  
   \[
   \frac{10 \text{ mL}}{100 \text{ mL}} \times 0.044 \text{ g} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]

4. **Convert grams to milligrams:**  
   \( 1 \text{ g} = 1000 \text{ mg} \).  
   So, \( 0.0044 \text{ g} = 0.0044 \times 1000 \text{ mg} = 4.4 \text{ mg} \).

**Final Answer:**  
There are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse.",relevance,"# Task Description
