To calculate the change in Gibbs free energy for the reaction, we use the formula:  
\[
\Delta G = n \Delta G_0^0
\]  
where \( \Delta G \) is the Gibbs free energy of the reaction, \( n \) is the number of moles of the product, and \( \Delta G_0^0 \) is the standard Gibbs free energy of formation of the product.  
The reaction is:  
\[
2 \text{H}_2 + \text{O}_2 \rightarrow 2 \text{H}_2\text{O}
\]  
