\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{1}{2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} = 5.0 \times 10^{23} \text{ MeV}
\]  

This uncertainty arises from the short lifetime of the particle, which limits the precision of its energy measurements. The uncertainty is on the order of \(10^{23} \text{ MeV}\), which is much larger than the rest energy of the particle.  

Thus, the typical range of outcomes for measurements of the Σ⁺ rest energy would be:  
\[
E = E_0 \pm \Delta E = 1385 \text{ MeV} \pm 5.0 \times 10^{23} \text{ MeV}
\]  

