   \[
   \text{Product} = s \times (s - a) \times (s - b) \times (s - c) = 25 \times 10 \times 10 \times 5 = 12500
   \]

4. **Take the square root of the product to find the area**:
   \[
   \text{Area} = \sqrt{12500} = 111.803 \text{ square units}
   \]

Thus, the area of the isosceles triangle is $\boxed{111.803}$ square units.
